+/**
+ * Compiles every pipeline already loaded from the on-disk cache, blocking until
+ * they are all ready.
+ *
+ * The cache is loaded at GPU init but compiled asynchronously, and a draw whose
+ * pipeline is not ready yet is dropped rather than delayed -- which is what makes
+ * a scene's first visit show missing geometry for a few seconds. Calling this
+ * before the first frame trades a one-off wait at startup for no pop-in at all.
+ * Returns how many pipelines were built; gives up after a timeout rather than
+ * hanging, leaving the rest to compile in the background as before.
+ */
+u32 AuroraPrecompilePipelines(void);
+
+/**
+ * How many pipelines loaded from the cache are still waiting to be created.
+ *
+ * Non-blocking, unlike AuroraPrecompilePipelines: the caller keeps driving its
+ * own frame loop and polls this, so the window stays responsive and can show
+ * progress rather than appearing to hang while the driver compiles.
+ */
+u32 AuroraPipelinesQueued(void);
